-- Tignes Val d'Isère: chapter and access revisions of 24 October 2026.
-- Run in the Supabase SQL editor for project xycfsimxicybvmwxbdfx. One transaction; the last query checks the result.
begin;
-- free the ords that move (access paras gain a third paragraph; the snowboard chapter gains a fourth)
update content.content_block set ord = ord + 100 where place_id='area:tignes-val-disere' and field in ('access.basesParas.0','access.basesParas.1');
with d as (select e->>0 field, e->>1 section, e->>2 slot, (e->>3)::int ord, e->>4 body from jsonb_array_elements($j$[["access.accessNote", "access", "note", 0, "Road distances are the fastest route by the OSRM router on OpenStreetMap data, without traffic or snow. The ski train as reported by <a href=\"https://www.seat61.com/trains-and-routes/eurostar-ski-train.htm\">Seat 61</a>; roads and buses by <a href=\"https://guide-ski.fr/?p=450\">Guide Ski</a>. Winter equipment rules: <a href=\"https://www.allopneus.com/guide-pratique/auto/conseils-pneu/loi-montagne-savoie\">Allopneus</a> (October 2026); parking: <a href=\"https://www.skiresort.com/en/ski-resort/tignes-val-disere/test-result/arrival-parking/\">skiresort.com</a>; Saturday traffic: <a href=\"https://www.alps2alps.com/blog/geneva-to-val-disere-transfer-cost\">Alps2Alps</a> (August 2026), a transfer company. 2026/27 bus timetables have not yet been checked."], ["access.basesParas.0", "access", "para", 3, "Tignes Le Lac and Val Claret are the best placed bases. From Val Claret, Val d'Isère is {{f:F000449|w}} lift rides away and a lift top above 3,000 m only {{f:F000451|w}}, by the Perce-Neige funicular. From the village of Val d'Isère, Tignes Le Lac is {{f:F000456|w}} lift rides away."], ["access.basesParas.1", "access", "para", 4, "Les Brévières and Le Fornet are quieter, and further from the rest of the area by lift. From Les Brévières, Val d'Isère takes {{f:F000465|w}} lift rides and Le Fornet {{f:F000466|w}}; from Le Fornet, Tignes Le Lac takes {{f:F000468|w}}."], ["chapters.0.paras.0", "snowboard", "para", 0, "Each resort keeps its own park. Tignes has its snowpark at the top of the Grattalu chair above Val Claret, with kickers, rails and boxes for beginners and intermediates and a free airbag, a halfpipe at the foot of the Lanches chair, and an expert boardercross in the same Palet sector. Val d'Isère's Val Park fills the middle of the Bellevarde bowl below the Mont Blanc chair, with kickers graded from green to black. In 2026 the Grande Motte glacier also opened for a month of summer skiing from late June, though SnowStash reports that most of it was on leftover winter snow."], ["chapters.0.paras.1", "snowboard", "para", 1, "Tignes keeps its off piste close to the lifts. See Tignes points to the trees off the Aiguille Percée chair above Les Brévières for days when the light goes flat, but warns that without a guide it is easy to end up stranded at the bottom. Higher up, a small bowl to the left of the Double M lift and the edges of the Grande Motte runs hold soft snow after a fall. Ski New Gen puts the Vallon de la Sache among its five favourite Tignes routes, a short hike from the chairs near the Aiguille Percée, with open ground and narrow couloirs all the way down to Les Brévières."], ["chapters.0.paras.2", "snowboard", "para", 2, "Val d'Isère has the better known routes. Ultimate France calls the Tour du Charvet, reached from the Grand Pré chair on Bellevarde, a good first off piste route for competent riders, and it runs through the Vanoise National Park. Above Le Fornet the Montet drag leads to the Col Pers, which the same guide rates suitable for every off piste level, and to the much steeper Pointe Pers. For poor visibility it recommends the steep, spaced trees below the Le Fornet cable car, and the Danaïdes woods above Le Laisinant offer jumps and drops between cliffs."], ["chapters.0.note", "snowboard", "note", 0, "Parks: <a href=\"https://seetignes.com/ski-area/snowparks\">See Tignes</a> (October 2024) and <a href=\"https://guide-ski.fr/?p=170\">Guide Ski</a>. Off piste: <a href=\"https://www.seetignes.com/ski-area/off-piste\">See Tignes</a> (October 2026), <a href=\"https://www.skinewgen.com/?p=110550\">Ski New Gen</a> and <a href=\"https://www.ultimatefrance.com/?p=8576\">Ultimate France</a> (December 2024). Summer skiing: <a href=\"https://snowstash.com/news/2026/07/tignes-grande-motte-glacier-summer-skiing\">SnowStash</a> (July 2026). Drag lift shares from OpenStreetMap. Park layouts change every season, and off piste routes need a guide and the day's avalanche bulletin."], ["chapters.2.paras.2", "food", "para", 2, "In Tignes, L'Alpage des Chaudannes and Lo Soli share the top of the Chaudannes chair above Le Lac and Le Lavachet. The first serves Savoyard dishes and Savoie wines on a sun terrace, and the second offers table service alongside a self service counter. In Val Claret, La Taverne des Neiges by the Bollin and Fresse chairs looks up at the Grande Motte, and Snowcarbon recommends Le Panoramic mainly for its views."], ["chapters.2.note", "food", "note", 0, "Michelin 2026: <a href=\"https://presse.explore-savoie.com/les-tables-distinguees-2026/\">Savoie tourism</a>. Restaurants: <a href=\"https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/val-disere/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife\">Snowcarbon</a> for Val d'Isère and for <a href=\"https://www.snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/tignes/tignes-eat-drink-party\">Tignes</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.seetignes.com/restaurants/mountain/\">See Tignes</a>. Restaurants change hands and menus each season."], ["chapters.3.note", "apres", "note", 0, "Sources: <a href=\"https://www.mon-sejour-en-montagne.com/histoires-et-anecdotes/la-folie-douce-a-val-d-isere-ce-restaurant-d-altitude-devenu-le-haut-lieu-de-la-fete-sur-les-pistes/\">Mon séjour en montagne on La Folie Douce</a> (September 2023), <a href=\"https://snowcarbon.co.uk/ski-resorts/val-disere/restaurants-apres-ski-nightlife\">Snowcarbon</a> and <a href=\"https://www.aluxurytravelblog.com/2021/11/25/apres-ski-bars-in-val-disere/\">A Luxury Travel Blog</a> (2021) for Val d'Isère, and <a href=\"https://www.igluski.com/blog/post/best-apres-ski-bars-and-nightlife-hotspots-in-tignes\">Iglu Ski</a> and <a href=\"https://www.seetignes.com/tignes-le-lavachet\">See Tignes</a> on <a href=\"https://www.seetignes.com/tignes-les-brevieres\">its villages</a> (October 2026) for Tignes. Bars open and close from season to season."], ["fit.catches", "fit", "line", 53, "The six day pass is the dearest of the four Savoie areas on this site, and neither resort offers a cheaper week of its own. The fewest lift rides back into Tignes Le Lac and Les Brévières from Val d'Isère use black runs, and Le Fornet depends on a single chair. Lower down, the modelled snow has thinned, with four of the last five seasons at 1,600 m in the lowest third."]]$j$::jsonb) e)
update content.content_block b set section=d.section, slot=d.slot, ord=d.ord, body=d.body, fact_refs=coalesce(array(select distinct x from regexp_matches(d.body, '\{\{(?:f|diff):([^}|]+)', 'g') m, unnest(string_to_array(m[1], ',')) x order by x), '{}')
from d where b.place_id='area:tignes-val-disere' and b.field=d.field;
insert into content.content_block (place_id,section,slot,ord,body,fact_refs,status,author,field)
select 'area:tignes-val-disere', e->>1, e->>2, (e->>3)::int, e->>4, coalesce(array(select distinct x from regexp_matches(e->>4, '\{\{(?:f|diff):([^}|]+)', 'g') m, unnest(string_to_array(m[1], ',')) x order by x), '{}'), 'review', 'loader', e->>0
from jsonb_array_elements($j$[["access.paras.2", "access", "para", 2, "Tignes and Val d'Isère fall under the Loi Montagne, which from November to March requires winter tyres on all four wheels or snow chains in the car. Both resorts charge for parking in garages and car parks, while Les Brévières has a free open car park for day visitors, according to skiresort.com. Alps2Alps, a transfer company, warns that Saturday changeovers bring long queues on the single lane stretches of the D902, and advises leaving the resort many hours before a Saturday flight."], ["chapters.0.paras.3", "snowboard", "para", 3, "Drag lifts are scarce in the villages and common on the glacier. In the map data {{f:F000413}} of the {{f:F000412}} main lifts are drags; they make up {{f:F000431}} of the main lifts on the Grande Motte and {{f:F000447}} in Le Fornet, against {{f:F000427}} in Val Claret. All of the terrain beyond the markers is uncontrolled, so the avalanche bulletin and a local guide come first."], ["chapters.2.paras.3", "food", "para", 3, "Down in the villages, Snowcarbon recommends Le Coeur des Neiges at Le Lac for tartiflette around fire pits, Le Caveau in Val Claret for home style Savoyard cooking, and Bazurto, also in Val Claret, for Colombian cooking on a special occasion. Les Brévières has the most traditional setting, with L'Armailly in a handsome chalet, and the restaurants at the foot of its slopes fill up at lunchtime."], ["chapters.3.paras.3", "apres", "para", 3, "The smaller villages are quieter. Le Lavachet has Le Brasero, a ski in, ski out bar with live music and burgers, and See Tignes describes the hamlet as local in feel and good for après. Les Brévières has a laid back scene built around its restaurants, and with no shuttle buses to the other villages, most people stay put once the lifts close."]]$j$::jsonb) e;
